{"_v":3,"id":"underdog-the-other-other-bronte-west-end-2024","cat":"west-end","cs":56.52,"rc":6,"bd":{"positive":0,"mixed":5,"negative":1},"rv":[{"cn":"Nick Curtis","o":"Evening Standard","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/underdog-the-other-other-bronte-national-theatre-review-b1149576.html","q":"This is slickly done, knockabout fun which takes on some serious subjects"},{"cn":"Arifa Akbar","o":"The Guardian","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2024/apr/05/underdog-the-other-other-bronte-review-national-theatre-london","d":"2024-04-05","q":"quick-witted and amusing...never deepens enough for the emotional punches to land."},{"cn":"Dominic Cavendish","o":"The Telegraph","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/theatre/what-to-see/underdog-the-other-other-bronte-national-theatre-review/","q":"I just feel it’s time to let the novels, in all their richness... speak for themselves."},{"cn":"Andrzej Lukowski","o":"Time Out London","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.timeout.com/london/theatre/underdog-the-other-bronte-review","q":"‘Underdog’ is a very funny play. That funniness doesn’t always work to its advantage."},{"cn":"Sam Marlowe","o":"The Stage","s":40,"b":"Negative","t":1,"u":"https://www.thestage.co.uk/reviews/underdog-the-other-other-bronte-review-national-theatre-london-sarah-gordon-rhiannon-clements-adele-james-gemma-whelan","q":"But as an exploration of women...it feels like a sadly wasted opportunity."},{"cn":"Sarah Crompton","o":"WhatsOnStage","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.whatsonstage.com/news/underdog-the-other-other-bronte-at-the-national-theatre-review_1590165/","q":"It’s written with passion and wit, yet somehow leaves its subjects diminished."}],"pd":"2024-03-27"}